prompts.body:
Write me an Excel formula.
- Table layout: {{표구조}}
- Result I want: {{원하는결과}}
- Result cell: {{결과칸}}
- Excel version: {{엑셀버전}}

1. A formula I can paste in
2. What it does, one line per part in plain words
3. Which parts need $ locking when I fill it down
4. When the result tends to go wrong and how to check it
5. A fallback formula if my version lacks a function

This formula returns a {{오류}} error. Give me the likely causes, most likely first, and a fixed formula.
Formula: {{수식}}
Situation: {{상황}}

Write me an Excel VBA macro.
- What it does (in order): {{작업순서}}
- Sheet name: {{시트이름}}
- Excel version: {{엑셀버전}}

1. VBA code to paste (a plain-English comment on every line)
2. Click-by-click steps to add and run it (starting from turning on the Developer tab)
3. Have it automatically create a backup sheet before running
4. If the data or sheet is missing, stop and show a message
5. Tell me how to save it (.xlsm)

Write a job posting for {{플랫폼}} using the information below.
- Company: {{회사소개}}
- Role: {{직무}}
- Main duties: {{주요업무}}
- Requirements: {{자격요건}}
- Terms: {{근무조건}}

Structure: 3 title options / one-line pitch / main duties / requirements & nice-to-haves / terms / hiring process
Use only the terms I gave you; mark anything missing as [CHECK]. Don't use wording that limits by gender, age or other protected traits.

Write an internal announcement.
- Type: {{종류}}
- Key points: {{내용}}
- For: {{대상}}
- Effective: {{시행일}}
- Questions: {{문의처}}

1. Formal notice (title, body, attachments line)
2. A chat/Slack version in 5 lines or less
Don't add benefits or conditions I didn't give; mark gaps as [CHECK].

Turn the notes below into meeting minutes.
- Meeting: {{회의명}}
- Date/time: {{일시}}
- Attendees: {{참석자}}

Structure: Overview / Discussion (by topic) / Decisions / Action items table (task, owner, due) / Parked items
Don't add anything not in the notes; if an owner or due date is missing, mark [CHECK].

Notes:
{{메모}}

Draft a {{규정명}} as a Word file.
- Purpose: {{목적}}
- Applies to: {{대상}}
- Must include: {{주요내용}}

1. Policy in numbered sections (purpose, definitions, scope, procedure, responsibilities, effective date)
2. A matching request form (table layout, with approval boxes)
3. Mark sections that need a legal check as [LEGAL CHECK]

[Output rules]
- Word (.docx), one clean page layout, standard business font
- Don't invent anything I didn't give you (numbers, dates, promises). Mark gaps as [CHECK].

Write the weekly report for {{기간}}. Short bullets, nothing that isn't in my notes.

This week:
{{한일}}

Next week:
{{계획}}

Issues & asks:
{{이슈}}

Write a business email.
- To: {{받는사람}}
- Purpose: {{목적}}
- Must include: {{내용}}
- Tone: {{톤}}

Give subject and body in two versions (a bit softer / a bit firmer). Don't add promises, dates or amounts I didn't give.

Write a reply to the email below. My position: '{{입장}}'. Answer everything they asked.

Their email:
{{받은메일}}

Write an Apps Script that sends emails automatically from a Google Sheet.
- Sheet name: {{시트이름}}
- Columns: {{열목록}}
- Subject: {{제목}}
- When to send: {{발송시점}}

1. Code (plain-English comments): send only rows where 'Sent' is blank, then record the send time
2. A 'test mode' setting at the top: when on, every email goes only to {{시험메일}}
3. Setup: from Extensions > Apps Script through to a time-driven trigger
4. Permission screens, daily send limits and how to check errors

Build a customer FAQ for a {{업종}}. Our policies:
{{정책}}

1. Group similar questions into 10–15 questions
2. For each, a short answer (2–3 lines for chat) and a formal answer (email)
3. Put questions policy can't answer in a separate 'Needs a person' list
Tone: {{톤}}

Questions:
{{문의}}
